Current 52000.0 profit 0.0

- Abstraction: Account monthlyProfit() ঘোষণা করে, কীভাবে হিসাব হবে তা বলে না।
- Encapsulation: balance private, শুধু add() দিয়ে বদলায়।
- Inheritance: Savings ও Current, Account-কে extend করে এর code পুনরায় ব্যবহার করে।
- Polymorphism: deposit() overload করা, আর monthlyProfit() override করা এবং run time-এ বাছাই হয়।

সুবিধা ও সীমাবদ্ধতা: এগুলো মিলে পুনর্ব্যবহার, data-র নিরাপত্তা ও সহজ সম্প্রসারণ দেয় (নতুন account type-এর জন্য পুরনো code বদলাতে হয় না)। খরচ হলো বেশি design পরিশ্রম ও কিছু run-time indirection, তাই বড় ও দীর্ঘমেয়াদি system-এই OOP সবচেয়ে লাভজনক।

model_answer_en:
Definition: A class is a blueprint (a user-defined type) that declares the fields and methods its objects will have. An object is an instance of that class: a block of memory holding one set of field values.

| Point | Class | Object |
|---|---|---|
| What it is | Blueprint, template, user-defined type | Instance of the class |
| Entity | Logical | Physical: occupies memory |
| How many | Declared once | Created many times |
| Created with | the class keyword | new (Java); Student s; also in C++ |
| Memory for fields | None (except static members) | Its own copy of every non-static field |
| Example | Student | s1 (Ayesha), s2 (Rafiq) |

Example

class Student {                      // class: written once, a blueprint
    String name;
    int roll;
    void show() { System.out.println(roll + ": " + name); }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Student s1 = new Student();  // object 1
        Student s2 = new Student();  // object 2, with its own name and roll
        s1.name = "Ayesha"; s1.roll = 1;
        s2.name = "Rafiq";  s2.roll = 2;
        s1.show();
        s2.show();
    }
}

Output:
1: Ayesha
2: Rafiq

One class Student gives two objects; each has its own name and roll, but both share the same show() code.

Remember: the class is the house plan and objects are the houses built from it.

