model_answer_en:
Abstraction: showing only the essential features of an object and hiding how they are carried out. It is a design decision about what the outside world needs, achieved with abstract classes, interfaces and public methods. Example: an SMS service exposes send(to, text) and hides the gateway, keys and retry logic.

Encapsulation: wrapping data and the methods that operate on it into one unit (a class) and restricting direct access to that data. Data hiding is its protective part: fields are private and change only through methods that check the rules.

| Point | Abstraction | Encapsulation |
|---|---|---|
| Question | What does it do? | How is it packed and guarded? |
| Level | Design | Implementation |
| Hides | Complexity | Data, by access control |
| Tool | Abstract class, interface | Class, private fields, getters/setters |
| Example | Sms.send() | private apiKey, sentToday in GatewaySms |

Example

abstract class Sms {                        // abstraction: callers see only send()
    public abstract boolean send(String to, String text);
}

class GatewaySms extends Sms {
    private String apiKey;                  // encapsulation + data hiding
    private int sentToday;
    GatewaySms(String key) { apiKey = key; }
    public boolean send(String to, String text) {
        if (text.length() > 160) return false;   // the rule stays inside the class
        sentToday++;
        System.out.println("To " + to + ": " + text);
        return true;
    }
    public int getSentToday() { return sentToday; }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Sms sms = new GatewaySms("k-123");
        sms.send("01711000000", "Your OTP is 4821");
        System.out.println(((GatewaySms) sms).getSentToday());
    }
}

Output:
To 01711000000: Your OTP is 4821
1

The caller programs against Sms (abstraction); apiKey and sentToday are private and change only inside send() (encapsulation).

Memory hook: abstraction is the menu, encapsulation is the kitchen door, data hiding is the lock on it.

