মনে রাখার কৌশল: abstraction হলো menu, encapsulation রান্নাঘরের দরজা, আর data hiding সেই দরজার তালা।

model_answer_en:
Definition: A functional interface is an interface with exactly one abstract method. Default and static methods have bodies and do not count. Because there is only one method to implement, an object of the interface can be written as a lambda expression or a method reference.

@FunctionalInterface: optional, but if present the compiler reports an error when the interface has zero or more than one abstract method.

| Built-in (java.util.function) | Abstract method | Typical use |
|---|---|---|
| Predicate<T> | boolean test(T t) | Validation, filtering |
| Function<T, R> | R apply(T t) | Transforming a value |
| Consumer<T> | void accept(T t) | forEach actions |
| Supplier<T> | T get() | Producing values lazily |
| Runnable (java.lang) | void run() | A task for a thread |

Example

import java.util.function.Predicate;

@FunctionalInterface
interface Discount {
    double apply(double price);                         // the single abstract method
    default Discount then(Discount next) {              // default methods are allowed
        return p -> next.apply(apply(p));
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Discount eid = p -> p * 0.90;                   // lambda
        Discount coupon = p -> p - 50;
        System.out.println(eid.apply(1000));
        System.out.println(eid.then(coupon).apply(1000));

        Predicate<String> validMobile = s -> s.matches("01[3-9]\\d{8}");   // built-in functional interface
        System.out.println(validMobile.test("01712345678"));
        System.out.println(validMobile.test("0123"));
    }
}

Output:
900.0
850.0
true
false

Benefit: short, readable behaviour passed as data (strategies, callbacks, stream operations) without writing a class for each. Limitation: a lambda fits only an interface with one abstract method, and long lambdas are harder to debug than named classes.

