model_answer_en:
Step 1: find the classes (nouns become classes, verbs become methods)

| Class | Main fields (private) | Main methods |
|---|---|---|
| Passenger (abstract) | name, nid | getName(), fare(base) (abstract) |
| Adult, Student | inherited | fare(base): full / half |
| Train | name, seatsLeft | reserveSeat(), getSeatsLeft() |
| Ticket | no, passenger, train, amount; static nextNo | toString() |
| BookingService | none | book(passenger, train, base) |

Step 2: class diagram

            Passenger (abstract)
            - name, nid
            + fare(base)
               ^          ^
               |          |       (inheritance: is-a)
             Adult     Student

  BookingService ---creates---> Ticket ---refers to---> Passenger
                                  |
                                  +------refers to----> Train
                                                        - seatsLeft
                                                        + reserveSeat()

Step 3: implementation

abstract class Passenger {
    private final String name;
    private final String nid;
    Passenger(String name, String nid) { this.name = name; this.nid = nid; }
    String getName() { return name; }
    abstract double fare(double base);          // each kind of passenger decides
}

class Adult extends Passenger {
    Adult(String n, String id) { super(n, id); }
    double fare(double base) { return base; }
}

class Student extends Passenger {
    Student(String n, String id) { super(n, id); }
    double fare(double base) { return base * 0.5; }
}

class Train {
    private final String name;
    private int seatsLeft;
    Train(String name, int seats) { this.name = name; this.seatsLeft = seats; }
    String getName() { return name; }
    boolean reserveSeat() {                      // the only way to change seatsLeft
        if (seatsLeft == 0) return false;
        seatsLeft--;
        return true;
    }
    int getSeatsLeft() { return seatsLeft; }
}

class Ticket {
    private static int nextNo = 1;
    private final int no;
    private final Passenger p;
    private final Train t;
    private final double amount;
    Ticket(Passenger p, Train t, double amount) {
        this.no = nextNo++; this.p = p; this.t = t; this.amount = amount;
    }
    public String toString() { return "Ticket " + no + ": " + p.getName() + ", " + t.getName() + ", Tk " + amount; }
}

class BookingService {
    Ticket book(Passenger p, Train t, double base) {
        if (!t.reserveSeat()) return null;       // no seat, no ticket
        return new Ticket(p, t, p.fare(base));
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Train subarna = new Train("Subarna Express", 2);
        BookingService svc = new BookingService();
        System.out.println(svc.book(new Adult("Rahim", "1990123456"), subarna, 800));
        System.out.println(svc.book(new Student("Mitu", "2004123456"), subarna, 800));
        System.out.println(svc.book(new Adult("Kamal", "1985123456"), subarna, 800));
        System.out.println("Seats left: " + subarna.getSeatsLeft());
    }
}

Output:
Ticket 1: Rahim, Subarna Express, Tk 800.0
Ticket 2: Mitu, Subarna Express, Tk 400.0
null
Seats left: 0

Step 4: OOP concepts used
- Encapsulation and data hiding: seatsLeft is private and changes only in reserveSeat(), which refuses at 0, so the count can never go negative.
- Abstraction: BookingService calls p.fare(base) without knowing the passenger type.
- Inheritance: Adult and Student reuse Passenger's fields and constructor.
- Polymorphism: fare() is overridden, so the right fare is chosen at run time (800 vs 400).
- Static member: Ticket.nextNo gives every ticket a unique number shared across all objects.

Extension: a new FreedomFighter passenger type is one more subclass; no existing class changes. Limitation: this core has no database or concurrency control; a real system must lock the seat count when many users book at once.

