Data requirements (all private, so the circle cannot be put into an invalid state)

| Field | Type | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| x, y | double | Centre of the circle; (0, 0) when it starts at the origin |
| radius | double | Must be positive; set once in the constructor |

Method requirements

| Method | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Circle(x, y, r), Circle(r) | Create a circle; reject r <= 0; the second starts at the origin |
| translate(dx, dy) | Move the centre by dx and dy |
| area() | Return pi r^2 |
| perimeter() | Return 2 pi r |
| getX(), getY(), getRadius() | Read the state without exposing the fields |

Data flow of translate(dx, dy)

caller --(dx, dy)--> translate()
    reads x, y  -->  x' = x + dx,  y' = y + dy  -->  writes x', y'
    radius is not touched, so area() and perimeter() give the same values

public class Circle {
    private double x;        // centre x
    private double y;        // centre y
    private double radius;

    public Circle(double x, double y, double radius) {
        if (radius <= 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException("radius must be positive");
        this.x = x;
        this.y = y;
        this.radius = radius;
    }

    public Circle(double radius) {       // a circle at the origin
        this(0, 0, radius);
    }

    // translation: move the centre by (dx, dy); the radius does not change
    public void translate(double dx, double dy) {
        x = x + dx;
        y = y + dy;
    }

    public double area()      { return Math.PI * radius * radius; }
    public double perimeter() { return 2 * Math.PI * radius; }
    public double getX()      { return x; }
    public double getY()      { return y; }
    public double getRadius() { return radius; }

    @Override
    public String toString() {
        return String.format("Circle[centre=(%.1f, %.1f), r=%.1f]", x, y, radius);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Circle c = new Circle(5);
        System.out.println(c);
        System.out.printf("Area = %.2f, Perimeter = %.2f%n", c.area(), c.perimeter());
        c.translate(3, 4);
        System.out.println(c);
        c.translate(-1, 2);
        System.out.println(c);
        System.out.printf("Area after moving = %.2f%n", c.area());
    }
}

Output:
Circle[centre=(0.0, 0.0), r=5.0]
Area = 78.54, Perimeter = 31.42
Circle[centre=(3.0, 4.0), r=5.0]
Circle[centre=(2.0, 6.0), r=5.0]
Area after moving = 78.54

